<title>GERMANY: German Intervention Board details EU sugar sales.</title>
<headline>German Intervention Board details EU sugar sales.</headline>
<dateline>FRANKFURT 1997-07-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>A total 52,600 tonnes of current series white sugar received export rebates of a maximum 39.600 European Currency Units (Ecus) per 100 kilos at the European Union tender, the German Intervention Board BLE said.</p>
<p>Out of the total, traders in France received 14,500 tonnes, in the UK received 25,000, in Germany 7,000, in Denmark 5,000 and in Finland 1,100, BLE said about the weekly event, held each Wednesday.</p>
<p>This week's award bring the cumulative tonnage for export from the 1996/97 crop to 2.494 million tonnes.</p>
<p>This week's result compared with 18,100 tonnes awarded on July 24, 1996, when the cumulative tonnage totalled 2.524 million tonnes.</p>
<p>Last week the EU awarded 24,000 tonnes of white sugar at a maximum rebate of 40.850 Ecus per 100 kilos.</p>
<p>-- Hamburg newsroom +49-40-41903275</p>
</text>
